# -DOFXPLUGIN_REQUIRE_ALL, both directions, Windows 2026-11-27.
#
# Four configures, two per template: the switch has to stop a packaging build where
# the default merely warns, and the default has to stay a warning so a machine
# without a toolkit can still configure the CPU path. Each block below is the
# tail of one configure log; the full logs stay in .validation/.
#
# The CUDA runs had every CUDA directory removed from PATH and CUDACXX cleared, so
# check_language(CUDA) finds nothing - the branch the option exists for. The
# inference runs used the CPU package (.validation/ort-1.32.0), which has no
# onnxruntime_providers_cuda, with OFXPLUGIN_BUNDLE_CUDA_PROVIDER=ON.

== CUDA template, OFXPLUGIN_ENABLE_CUDA=ON, no CUDA on PATH, -DOFXPLUGIN_REQUIRE_ALL=ON ==
  OFXPLUGIN_ENABLE_CUDA=ON but no CUDA compiler was found.
    OFXPLUGIN_REQUIRE_ALL=ON: this build asked for the component, so a configure that skips it would produce an artifact that is missing what the build was for. Drop the option that asked for it, or set -DOFXPLUGIN_REQUIRE_ALL=OFF if a partial build is what you want.
-- Configuring incomplete, errors occurred!

== the same configure with the option off ==
  OFXPLUGIN_ENABLE_CUDA=ON but no CUDA compiler was found.
